cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Finger Millet Drought Transcriptome — Reference-Guided
  Reanalysis (corrected)
message: >-
  If you use this dataset, please cite it using the metadata
  in this file. Please also cite the underlying RNA-seq data
  (Hatakeyama et al. 2018) and the reference genome assembly
  GCA_032690845.1, which are third-party works not covered by
  this deposit's licences. This deposit is dual-licensed: MIT
  for executable code (everything in scripts/, plus
  workflow/Snakefile and workflow/setup.sh) and CC BY 4.0 for
  all data, figures, documentation and workflow/config.yaml.
  See LICENSE for the full texts and the exact split.
type: dataset
authors:
  - given-names: Joash Joshua
    family-names: Ayo
    orcid: 'https://orcid.org/0009-0007-1642-0172'
    affiliation: Independent Researcher, Kampala, Uganda
    email: joashjoshua789@gmail.com
    city: Kampala
    country: UG
abstract: >-
  Reference-guided reanalysis of published drought-response
  RNA-seq data in finger millet (Eleusine coracana (L.)
  Gaertn.) against the chromosome-scale KNE 796-S genome
  assembly (GCA_032690845.1), which resolves both subgenomes
  of the allotetraploid into 18 pseudomolecules.


  The deposit contains TWO analyses. results_v2/ is the
  corrected re-analysis and supersedes results_v1/, which is
  the original April 2026 analysis retained unmodified as a
  historical record. Four defects were found in the original
  by audit and are documented in full: DESeq2 was supplied
  per-base coverage rescaled by 100 rather than read counts;
  the BLASTx annotation join never matched because bedtools
  getfasta wrote the GTF feature type as the FASTA name; the
  tier classifier matched stress keywords as substrings rather
  than words; and sequence extraction lost exon structure, so
  extracted sequences retain their introns.


  Corrected results: 21,864 novel intergenic transcripts
  (gffcompare class u) were detected, of which 2,422 are
  significantly drought-upregulated (adjusted p < 0.05,
  log2 fold change >= 1.5) using prepDE.py count matrices
  validated against featureCounts at Spearman rho 0.985-0.995.
  Of those, 1,532 (63.3 per cent) have no UniProt/Swiss-Prot
  homolog at E <= 1e-5, a rate consistent with published
  expectations for intergenic transcribed regions in the
  grasses rather than evidence of an unusual gene repertoire.
  203 (8.4 per cent) are mobile-element derived.


  One candidate, MSTRG.31255.1, survives systematic
  re-examination: a single-exon locus on chromosome 6A
  encoding a 104-amino-acid cysteine-rich peptide with a
  predicted signal peptide and extracellular localisation
  (log2FC 4.434, adjusted p 1.56e-32). It has no Swiss-Prot
  hit under the corrected join, but its ColabFold multiple
  sequence alignment contains 27 distinct homologs across
  seven grass genera and three subfamilies, all unreviewed
  TrEMBL entries. Homoeologous copies exist on 6A and 6B plus
  a tandem paralog on 6A. Its AlphaFold2 model is low
  confidence (mean pLDDT 59.95, pTM 0.390, MSA depth 34).


  The package includes the Snakemake workflow, maintained and
  recovered analysis scripts, both result sets, count
  matrices, corrected BLASTx output and annotation tables,
  ColabFold structural models with their MSAs and confidence
  scores, diagnostic figures, run logs, and documentation of
  provenance, corrections and known limitations. Treatment is
  confounded with plant age: control and drought tissue were
  sampled seven days apart and no time-matched well-watered
  control was sampled at day seven. Whether the two groups
  derive from the same individual plants cannot be established
  from either the data or the surviving experimental records,
  so the six libraries are treated as independent samples. The
  three libraries per condition come from separate plants, so
  the replication is biological rather than technical, although
  the archive metadata does not record this; between-replicate
  dispersion is extreme. The work is computational only and has
  not been peer reviewed.
keywords:
  - Eleusine coracana
  - finger millet
  - drought stress
  - RNA-seq
  - transcriptome
  - differential expression
  - novel gene annotation
  - intergenic transcribed regions
  - allotetraploid
  - orphan crop
  - reference-guided assembly
  - reproducibility
  - reanalysis
license:
  - MIT
  - CC-BY-4.0
version: 2.0.0
date-released: '2026-08-28'
